<title>USA: Merrill to pay $30 mln to end Calif. probe.</title>
<headline>Merrill to pay $30 mln to end Calif. probe.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co agreed Thursday to pay $30 million to settle a 2-1/2-year investigation by the Orange County, Calif., district attorney's office into the county's 1994 bankruptcy.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch also agreed to institute &quot;enhanced procedures for internal coordination&quot; on certain California municipal bond offerings, according to a company statement.</p>
</text>
